font-to-outline — measured proof of the invocation defect and its fix
=====================================================================
Reproduce with (every command is in this repo; fixtures land in a directory you
choose, nothing here is retyped from memory):

  0  python3 docs/research/font-outline-fixtures.py /tmp/fo-fix
  1  BROWSERSNIP_GS_DUMP=docs/research/font-outline-argv.json \
       npx vitest run tests/pdf/font-outline.test.ts
       # dumps the argv the SOURCE builds, from src/lib/pdf/core/engine-ops.ts
  2  node docs/research/font-outline-wasm.mjs docs/research/font-outline-argv.json <in.pdf> <outdir>
       # replays each vector through the published engine twice: as built, and with
       # the output switch split back into two arguments (the shape until 4ad2be3)
  3  python3 docs/research/font-outline-readers.py <in.pdf> <out.pdf> …
       # measures the result with engines that did not write it

Run 2026-11-11 in the BrowserSnip sandbox. Node v26.12.1, vitest 4.1.9, the
engine the tab downloads (`@bentopdf/gs-wasm@0.1.1`, GPL Ghostscript 10.06.0).

STEP 1 — the argv, quoted from both builds of src/lib/pdf/core/engine-ops.ts
  pre  = 4ad2be3~1 (docs/research/font-outline-argv.pre-4ad2be3.json)
  post = 4ad2be3   (docs/research/font-outline-argv.json)
  The only difference is where the output path sits relative to its switch.

textToOutlines (font-to-outline)
  pre  : ["-dQUIET", "-dNOPAUSE", "-dBATCH", "-dSAFER", "-sDEVICE=pdfwrite", "-dNoOutputFonts", "-dCompatibilityLevel=1.7", "-dAutoRotatePages=/None", "-dColorConversionStrategy=/LeaveColorUnchanged", "-sOutputFile", "/tmp/output.pdf", "/tmp/input.pdf"]
  post : ["-dQUIET", "-dNOPAUSE", "-dBATCH", "-dSAFER", "-sDEVICE=pdfwrite", "-dNoOutputFonts", "-dCompatibilityLevel=1.7", "-dAutoRotatePages=/None", "-dColorConversionStrategy=/LeaveColorUnchanged", "-sOutputFile=/tmp/output.pdf", "/tmp/input.pdf"]
  diff : ["-sOutputFile", "-sOutputFile=/tmp/output.pdf", "/tmp/output.pdf"]

convertToPdfA (pdf-to-pdfa)
  pre  : ["-dQUIET", "-dNOPAUSE", "-dBATCH", "-dSAFER", "-dPARANOIDSAFER", "-dPDFA=2", "-dPDFACompatibilityPolicy=1", "-sDEVICE=pdfwrite", "-dCompatibilityLevel=1.7", "-dAutoRotatePages=/None", "-dColorImageDownsampleType=/Bicubic", "-dColorImageResolution=300", "-dGrayImageResolution=300", "-dMonoImageResolution=600", "-dEmbedAllFonts=true", "-dSubsetFonts=true", "-dDetectDuplicateImages=true", "-dCompressFonts=true", "-sOutputFile", "/tmp/output.pdf", "/tmp/input.pdf"]
  post : ["-dQUIET", "-dNOPAUSE", "-dBATCH", "-dSAFER", "-dPARANOIDSAFER", "-dPDFA=2", "-dPDFACompatibilityPolicy=1", "-sDEVICE=pdfwrite", "-dCompatibilityLevel=1.7", "-dAutoRotatePages=/None", "-dColorImageDownsampleType=/Bicubic", "-dColorImageResolution=300", "-dGrayImageResolution=300", "-dMonoImageResolution=600", "-dEmbedAllFonts=true", "-dSubsetFonts=true", "-dDetectDuplicateImages=true", "-dCompressFonts=true", "-sOutputFile=/tmp/output.pdf", "/tmp/input.pdf"]
  diff : ["-sOutputFile", "-sOutputFile=/tmp/output.pdf", "/tmp/output.pdf"]

rebuildWithGhostscript (repair)
  pre  : ["-dQUIET", "-dNOPAUSE", "-dBATCH", "-dSAFER", "-sDEVICE=pdfwrite", "-dCompatibilityLevel=1.7", "-dAutoFixDirtyXrefTables=true", "-dDoThumbnails=false", "-sOutputFile", "/tmp/output.pdf", "/tmp/input.pdf"]
  post : ["-dQUIET", "-dNOPAUSE", "-dBATCH", "-dSAFER", "-sDEVICE=pdfwrite", "-dCompatibilityLevel=1.7", "-dAutoFixDirtyXrefTables=true", "-dDoThumbnails=false", "-sOutputFile=/tmp/output.pdf", "/tmp/input.pdf"]
  diff : ["-sOutputFile", "-sOutputFile=/tmp/output.pdf", "/tmp/output.pdf"]

Reading of STEP 1, against what docs/TOOL-TRIAGE.md item 3 inferred:

  The bug is NOT a difference between the `font-to-outline` vector and the
  working `pdf-to-pdfa` vector. All THREE vectors split `-sOutputFile` from its
  path, and all three exit 1 with the same sentence. `pdf-to-pdfa` only looked
  healthy because it carries a local fallback that wrote the file its card then
  attributed to Ghostscript — see STEP 2, and `ResultCard`'s Engine row, which
  prints `tool.engines[0]` (what a tool declares) and not what ran.

